Package: DelphiR
Type: Package
Title: Statistical Analysis of Delphi Studies
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Yuri", "Calleo", , "yuri.calleo@unimercatorum.it", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Tools for the statistical analysis of Delphi studies. Expert
    ratings collected over one or more rounds and on one or more indicators,
    such as impact and plausibility, are imported from spreadsheets or survey
    exports, validated against the rating scale and summarised through
    descriptive statistics, panel participation and item-level dispersion
    measures. Consensus is assessed with the interquartile-range criterion
    reviewed by von der Gracht (2012) <doi:10.1016/j.techfore.2012.04.013>,
    and stability between rounds with the Wilcoxon test or with a net-change
    criterion based on Scheibe, Skutsch and Schofer (1975). Items are then
    classified as consensus, unstable consensus, stable dissent or open, in
    order to identify those to be submitted to a further round. The package
    also provides data-entry templates, publication-quality figures and
    self-contained round reports in HTML or 'Microsoft Word' format.
